Both scripts have a hand-written =head1 NAME / =head1 SYNOPSIS block right after __END__, and ALSO get a PodWeaver-generated NAME (from # PODNAME + # ABSTRACT) inserted at the very top of the POD, ahead of VERSION. Confirmed in the built tarball:

bin/hcloud.pl -- =head1 NAME appears at line 116 (generated, followed by VERSION/SYNOPSIS) and again at line 169 (hand-written, right before OPTIONS), both saying "hcloud.pl - Hetzner Cloud CLI (Perl implementation)".
bin/hrobot.pl -- same pattern, lines 19 and 54.

podchecker does not flag this (duplicate headings are not a syntax error) but metacpan/POD-to-HTML renders two NAME entries in the table of contents. Pre-existing, not introduced by the current diff.

Fix: delete the second, hand-written "=head1 NAME\n\n<script> - ..." block in each file (the SYNOPSIS/DESCRIPTION/OPTIONS content below/around it stays; only the duplicate NAME heading needs to go).

